%N A115568 Maximum Fibonacci exponent in prime factorization of n, or 1 if there is no Fibonacci exponent.
%C A115568 From _Amiram Eldar_, Sep 19 2026: (Start)
%C A115568 Let f(k) = Product_{p prime} (1 - Sum_{i > k} 1/p^Fibonacci(i) - 1/p^(Fibonacci(i)+1)).
%C A115568 The asymptotic density of numbers n such that a(n) = Fibonacci(k) for k >= 2, is d(k) = f(k) - [k > 2] * f(k-1), where [ ] is the Iverson bracket.
%C A115568 The asymptotic density of numbers without Fibonacci exponents is 0 (they are all 4-full numbers, A036967).
%C A115568 The asymptotic mean of this sequence is lim_{m->oo} (1/m) * Sum_{k=1..m} a(k) = Sum_{k>=2} d(k) * Fibonacci(k) = 1.51093734684523345129... . (End)
%H A115568 Antti Karttunen, <a href="/A115568/b115568.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A115568 <a href="/index/Eu#epf">Index entries for sequences computed from exponents in factorization of n</a>.
%t A115568 Module[{fibs=Fibonacci[Range[10]]},Table[Max[Select[FactorInteger[n][[All,2]],MemberQ[fibs,#]&]]/.(-\[Infinity]->1),{n,100}]] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Apr 08 2022 *)
%o A115568 (PARI)
%o A115568 A010056(n) = { my(k=n^2); k+=(k+1)<<2; issquare(k) || (n>0 && issquare(k-8)); } \\ This function from _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Jul 30 2012
%o A115568 A115568(n) = { my(exps=factorint(n)[, 2], expswith1 = vector(1+length(exps),i,if(1==i,i,exps[i-1]))); vecmax(apply(e -> (A010056(e)*e), expswith1)); }; \\ _Antti Karttunen_, Jul 23 2017
